    "faq_fFAwqm": {
      "type": "faq",
      "blocks": {
        "text_XEPM9x": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Are these genuinely pure shilajit tablets or is pure just on the label?",
            "answer": "<p>No fillers. No binders. No synthetic excipients. Raw shilajit resin from Nepal's Everest region, extracted, dried using traditional methods, and compressed into a 250mg tablet. Every batch is independently tested by Certified Laboratories, accredited to ISO/IEC 17025:2017 — fulvic acid content, heavy metals, microbial purity. Three separate reports, all on record. The Certificate of Analysis is available on this page. That is what pure actually means.</p>"
          }
        },
        "text_gDQ9Fy": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What exactly do you mean by Himalayan shilajit tablets? Where is it from?",
            "answer": "<p>Solukhumbu (the Everest region), Dolpa, Darchula, and Humla — all in Nepal — at altitudes of 16,000–18,000 feet. Not Himalayan as a label. Himalayan as a precise location with a name, an altitude, a season, and a community of people who harvest it. <br/></p>"
          }
        },
        "text_agVMCY": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What makes these the best shilajit tablets to buy?",
            "answer": "<p>Three things: source, formula, and proof. Our shilajit is sourced from the Everest region of Nepal, above 18,000 ft — not blended from unspecified origins. Each tablet contains pure shilajit extract, with nothing added to bind, bulk, or increase the weight. And every batch is supported by three independent lab reports from Certified Laboratories.</p>"
          }
        },
        "text_kfYyPC": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How long before I notice results from shilajit tablets?",
            "answer": "<p>Most customers reach out somewhere between weeks three and ten. The compounds in pure Himalayan shilajit tablets, fulvic acid, 85+ trace minerals, Dibenzo-α-Pyrones, work cumulatively. The daily dose builds over time. We recommend a minimum of 30 days before evaluating. Consistency is the only variable that matters.</p>"
          }
        },
        "text_krnBRN": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Are these the same as shilajit tablets and shilajit dry drops?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. Shilajit dry drops and shilajit tablets are the same product. Pure shilajit extract, 250mg per tablet, same source, same lab, same standard. Dry Drops is simply the format name we use for our tablet form. Same origin. Same proof. Different name for the same thing.</p>"
          }
        },
        "text_dqHkbL": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Why does price matter? Is cheaper shilajit not the same?",
            "answer": "<p>The cost of producing genuine pure shilajit tablets is not a mystery. High-altitude harvesting by licensed collectors. Minimal processing to preserve the raw composition. Independent lab testing, three separate reports per batch from an ISO/IEC 17025:2017 accredited laboratory. SGS GMP certification, renewed through external audit. Each of these has a real cost. The price of the tablet reflects what went into making it verifiable, not just sellable.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
